  "term": "International Phonetic Alphabet",
  "definition": "In this context, the International Phonetic Alphabet is a form of phonetic transcription used to represent spoken language for analysis. In neurolinguistic assessment tools, converting speech or text into this format helps support pronunciation and phonology analysis.",
